INT. GENERATION SHIP "HALCYON REACH" - HYDROPONICS RING - SHIP'S NIGHT

A curved corridor of green. Racks of lettuce and soy climb the walls under violet grow-lamps. Condensation beads on every pipe. Far below the deck plates, the ship's engines pulse like a slow heart.

COMMANDER ISOLDE VARGAS-ABIOLA, fifties, stands at a junction with her arms folded, still in her night robe. Her first officer, TOMASZ BRZEZINSKI, forties, has a hand tablet and a scowl. The agronomist, DR. NADIA OKONKWO-REID, thirties, kneels at a rack with a soil probe. The boy, KAI SOLOMON, twelve, lingers behind a tank with a bucket. A maintenance tech, FEODOR LINDGREN, sixty, sits cross-legged on the deck with a panel open. And the ship's counselor, PRIYANKA ADEYEMI, forties, hangs back at the corridor mouth.

The grow-lamps flicker. Every leaf in the corridor turns, slowly, toward the same direction.

ISOLDE
Tell me that isn't what I think it is.

NADIA
It's phototropism. Plants turn toward light.

ISOLDE
There is no light there.

NADIA
No. There isn't.

Tomasz looks up from his tablet. Feodor taps his panel, and a weak amber glow pulses from the wiring. He snatches his hand away. Kai edges closer to the tank.

TOMASZ
Commander, the sensors show the hull is clear. No breach. No micrometeorites.

ISOLDE
Then why are my lettuces looking at the aft bulkhead?

FEODOR
Something's behind it.

TOMASZ
There's nothing behind it. It's a bulkhead.

FEODOR
Then something's inside it.

PRIYANKA
(softly)
Perhaps we should all take a breath.

ISOLDE
I'm breathing, Priyanka. It isn't helping.

Kai steps out from behind the tank, bucket swinging.

KAI
Mother says the walls have been singing since the last jump.

ISOLDE
Kai, go to your quarters.

KAI
I'm not afraid.

ISOLDE
I didn't say you were.

NADIA
Commander. The plants aren't only turning. Look at the stems. They're growing toward it. Measurably, in real time.

She holds up the probe. A readout glows. Tomasz crosses to her side, looks at it, and goes pale.

TOMASZ
That's twenty centimeters in five minutes.

NADIA
It's accelerating.

The corridor hums. A low tone rises in the deck plates. The violet lamps dim. And from the aft bulkhead, through the steel, a pale seam of light begins to spread, slow as water, ruffling every leaf.

TOMASZ
Is that...

NADIA ^
It's alive.

Tomasz and Nadia speak at the same time, their words overlapping, and then stop, each turning toward the other. Isolde steps forward, one hand lifted as if to touch the light.

ISOLDE
Nobody move.

Priyanka crosses herself in the old way. Feodor scrambles to his feet. Kai drops the bucket, and it clangs, and the sound echoes down the corridor and returns altered, almost a word.

KAI
(whispering)
It said "hello."

ISOLDE
Kai.

KAI
It did. It said hello.

Isolde kneels beside the boy and takes him by the shoulders.

ISOLDE
Kai, look at me. Did you hear anything else?

KAI
It said it was lonely.

Silence. The light stops spreading. A single tendril of green curls out from the nearest rack and brushes the boy's sleeve, gentle as a child's hand.

ISOLDE
Tomasz. Seal the corridor. Priyanka, get the captain. Nadia.

NADIA
Yes, Commander?

ISOLDE
Find out what it wants.

NADIA
And if it wants nothing?

ISOLDE
Then we will be very polite to it.

Isolde rises, and the seam of light flickers once in answer, and every leaf in the corridor turns to face her.
